_id":3,"text":" The New Jersey Devils defeated the defending champion Dallas Stars for their second Stanley Cup championship.","title":"1999–2000 NHL season"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" During the regular season, no player reached the 100-point plateau, the first time this had happened in a non-lockout season since the 1967–68 season.","title":"1999–2000 NHL season"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Also, in the 2000 Stanley Cup playoffs, the New Jersey Devils overcame a three games to one deficit against the Philadelphia Flyers to win the Eastern Conference Finals.","title":"1999–2000 NHL season"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" This was the first time that this had happened this late in the playoffs also since the 1967–68 season.","title":"1999–2000 NHL season"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 1999–2000 Colorado Avalanche season was the Avalanche's fifth season.","title":"1999–2000 Colorado Avalanche season"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was the first season in the new Pepsi Center arena.","title":"1999–2000 Colorado Avalanche season"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: The 1999 Galtür avalanche happened first.
